  <!-- ABOUT -->
  <section id="about">
    <h2 class="section-title">About</h2>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="body-text">
        <p>
          Born in Keriye (Uyghur region) in 1992, Erpan Hesher formed his first music ensemble in Beijing in 2008
          and quickly became their producer. Between 2009 and 2013 he played a key role in the first underground
          electronic scene in Urumchi – a movement that turned the city into one of the most vibrant hubs for real
          underground electronic music in China.
        </p>
        <p>
          In the following years he co-founded the independent collective <strong>Rock Family</strong> in Shanghai,
          organised more than a hundred events (including the ART MIX Festival), and launched the electronic duo
          <strong>NONE SOUNDS</strong>, bringing contemporary Uyghur music to international stages.
        </p>
        <p>
          After studying sound design and modular synthesis in Tokyo (MI Tokyo) from 2016 to 2018, he relocated to
          Europe, first in Serbia then in France, where he now lives in artistic exile. His work has expanded into
          electronic performance, sound art and music production, collaborating with choreographers, film-makers,
          writers, cultural institutions and heritage sites.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today, as an Artist Associate at Les Dominicains de Haute-Alsace and a NORA laureate within the ACCR
          network, he develops projects that intertwine modular sound, archives, cinema, architecture and
          narratives of displacement.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="body-text muted">
        <p><strong>Based in:</strong> France (working internationally)</p>
        <p><strong>Background:</strong> Uyghur artist in exile, electronic musician, sound artist, composer</p>
        <p><strong>Practice:</strong> live modular sets, immersive sound, cine-concerts, AV performances, film &amp; theatre scores</p>
        <p><strong>Languages:</strong> English, French, Uyghur, Chinese</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROJECTS / LIVE -->
  <section id="projects">
    <h2 class="section-title">Live &amp; Projects</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card">
        <small>Ciné-concert</small>
        <h3>Nosferatu (Murnau, 1922) – Live score</h3>
        <p>
          88-minute original electronic score for Murnau’s silent classic, performed live with modular synthesis.
          Presented at Les Dominicains de Haute-Alsace, with multiple dates scheduled (including student and public
          performances) and interest from other cultural centres and cinemas.
        </p>
        <div class="pill-row">
          <span class="pill">Modular live</span>
          <span class="pill">Silent cinema</span>
          <span class="pill">Tour-ready</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <small>Immersive concert &amp; orchestral collaboration</small>
        <h3>Novembre dans l’Âme</h3>
        <p>
          A meditative concert in memory of war victims, created with the Conservatoire de Colmar and Les Dominicains.
          Erpan composed the immersive electronic sound design, transitions and atmospheres around works by Ravel,
          Barraine, Gossec, Pärt and Mozart for performances at Les Dominicains and the Comédie de Colmar.
        </p>
        <div class="pill-row">
          <span class="pill">Orchestra + electronics</span>
          <span class="pill">Immersive sound</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <small>Ambient / AV</small>
        <h3>Relax Max – towards album &amp; AV tour</h3>
        <p>
          An immersive audiovisual project originally created at Les Dominicains, now becoming the core of Erpan’s
          first album and a touring AV concert. The music, built as a narrative soundtrack, will be reworked with
          live strings and piano, and adapted visually in collaboration with Jérôme Jean.
        </p>
        <div class="pill-row">
          <span class="pill">Album in development</span>
          <span class="pill">AV performance</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <small>Heritage &amp; site-specific</small>
        <h3>Ballersdorf – Orion et le Scorpion</h3>
        <p>
          Original soundtrack for a historical and regional project about the youth of Ballersdorf during World War II,
          soon to be presented at the Strasbourg Planetarium. A meditation on memory, testimony and rural history.
        </p>
        <div class="pill-row">
          <span class="pill">Heritage</span>
          <span class="pill">Narrative sound</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <small>Installation</small>
        <h3>Les Deux Merveilles &amp; Résonances Célestes</h3>
        <p>
          Long-form sound compositions for audiovisual and architectural installations at Les Dominicains,
          exploring celestial themes, light and the resonance of the site through ambient and experimental electronics.
        </p>
        <div class="pill-row">
          <span class="pill">Site-specific</span>
          <span class="pill">Installation</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <small>Multidisciplinary performance</small>
        <h3>Cauchemar / Qoshmaq (in creation)</h3>
        <p>
          A multidisciplinary project blending electronic music, Uyghur tradition, theatre, poetry and visual scenography.
          Developed with ACCR (NORA), INA and SOAS University of London, it reflects on dreams, exile and collective memory.
        </p>
        <div class="pill-row">
          <span class="pill">NORA / ACCR</span>
          <span class="pill">Hybrid performance</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FILMS & SOUNDTRACKS -->
